       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 skip mg. The main risk at this level is lactic acidosis, and it applies even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I can enter it with a note recording that it was intentional, though I'd advise against it."
